-- title:
--   Fourteen-step Syracuse descent on chunk 4 of the modulus-$2^{23}$ refinement (2313 residue classes)
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)$ be the odd part of $3n+1$ (the platform's Syracuse map `syracuseStep`), and let $T^{14}$ denote fourteen successive applications. Let $R_{4}$ be the explicit list of 2313 distinct residues modulo $2^{23}=8388608$ enumerated in the formal statement. For every natural number $n$,
--
--   $$
--   n\bmod 8388608\in R_{4}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad T^{14}(n)<n.
--   $$
--
--   This is chunk 4 of 10 of the modulus-$2^{23}$ refinement of the [fifteen-branch residual after the step-12 refinement](https://prove2.me/theorems/94e7a593-755c-4790-baa9-9df502e646d3); the ten chunks are disjoint and together cover 23124 residue classes, all lying over the leaf's 69159 surviving classes modulo $2^{22}$, each admitting a descent certificate with exponent budget $23$. Every listed residue satisfies $r\equiv 15\pmod{16}$ and avoids all earlier exclusion lists of the branch.
--
--   **Method.** For each $r\in R_{4}$ the first thirteen Syracuse steps of $r$ are exact rows $3b_k+1=2^{a_k}b_{k+1}$ with $b_0=r$ and odd $b_{k+1}$, with $S=\sum_{k<13}a_k\le 23$, and the fourteenth row is closed by a divisor exponent $e=\min(v_2(3b_{13}+1),\,23-S)$ with quotient $B=(3b_{13}+1)/2^{e}<r$. The published theorem [`CollatzFrontier.syracuse_terminal_budget_of_descent`](https://prove2.me/theorems/2513a4d3-77eb-4b93-9876-33755812122c) then gives $T^{14}(r+2^{23}q)<r+2^{23}q$ for all $q$. The chunk is checked by one kernel evaluation of the checker over its literal list, so the 23124-class refinement is split into ten independently checked theorems.
--
--   **Role.** Together with the other nine chunks and the refined residual `syracuse_descent_residual_fifteen_mod16_mod1048576_after_step14_mod8388608` it reduces the open frontier leaf [`syracuse_descent_residual_fifteen_mod16_mod1048576_refined`](https://prove2.me/theorems/94e7a593-755c-4790-baa9-9df502e646d3) by a case split on membership in the ten chunk lists; the ten chunks together remove $23124/138318\approx 16.7\%$ of the leaf's open classes without bounding the starting value or the descent time.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The map is the existing definition `syracuseStep`; the residue list is a literal `List ℕ` inside the theorem's type, as in the earlier list theorems of this branch. The recursion-depth option only supports elaboration of the long literal. No monotonicity of the Syracuse map is asserted.
